 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+The worker implements 2Q eviction. The cache is partitioned into two LRU queues: A1 for first-use entries and A2 for entries accessed at least twice. A first cache hit for a key inserts the entry into A1; a subsequent hit moves the entry from A1 to A2 and promotes its recency. Hits within A2 update recency within A2. Eviction removes from A1 first, then from A2, protecting reused comparison sheets from one-off screening scans. The A1/A2 size split is a tunable parameter. All replacement bookkeeping remains private to the preview worker and does not change the external HTTP contract, render queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q with A1/A2 split | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | 2Q protects reused comparison sheets from sequential screening scans with acceptable bookkeeping. LRU has lowest cost but evicts useful sheets during long scans. Frequency with aging retains yesterday's favorites too long and adds counter maintenance. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. ✅ Eviction policy selected as 2Q
+
+### Deferred
+1. Exact A1/A2 size split value to be tuned during pilot.
+
